(Watering) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Water early in the morning so that leaves dry during the day, which reduces fungal disease.) Tj T*
(Push a finger two centimetres into the mix: if it feels dry, water slowly until water runs out) Tj T*
(of the drainage holes.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In peak Indian summer, terracotta pots may need watering twice a day, while plastic pots hold) Tj T*
(moisture longer. A layer of mulch, such as dry leaves or coconut husk, cuts evaporation) Tj T*
(noticeably.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Overwatering is a more common beginner mistake than underwatering. Yellowing lower leaves and a) Tj T*
(sour smell from the soil are typical signs of too much water.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Feeding plants) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Container plants exhaust their nutrients quickly. Add a handful of vermicompost to each pot) Tj T*
(every three weeks during the growing season. For fruiting plants, a liquid feed made by soaking) Tj T*
(banana peels in water for two days adds potassium, which helps flowering and fruit set.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
