(Pests and problems) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Aphids are tiny green or black insects that cluster on new growth. Spray them off with water,) Tj T*
(or apply a neem oil solution made from 5 ml of neem oil and a few drops of liquid soap in one) Tj T*
(litre of water, every five days in the evening.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Mealybugs look like white cotton on stems; dab them with a cotton swab dipped in rubbing) Tj T*
(alcohol. Remove leaves with powdery mildew promptly and improve air circulation between pots.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What to grow first) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For a first season, start with plants that forgive mistakes: mint, curry leaf, cherry tomatoes,) Tj T*
(green chillies and spinach. Microgreens such as mustard and radish can be harvested in about) Tj T*
(ten days, which makes them a rewarding first project.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Keep a simple notebook of sowing dates, watering and harvests. After one season you will know) Tj T*
(your balcony's sunlight and microclimate far better than any guide can tell you.) Tj T*
ET
